      "title": "Note: MiniMax Music 3",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Text to music — MiniMax Music 3\n\nWrite a **Caption** (what the song is) and **Lyrics** (what it sings), press **Run**, and a\nfinished song lands in your bucket as `song_00001_.mp3`, `song_00002_.mp3`, ... The save\ncounter never overwrites, so every take is kept and you pick the good ones later.\n\n### The two inputs do different jobs\n\n| Box | What it controls |\n|---|---|\n| **Caption** | Everything about the sound. Write it in three sections in this order — `Global Metadata:` (genre, BPM, key, mood, use case, production texture), `Vocal Details:` (voice type, delivery, harmonies), `Arrangement:` (instruments, and what happens in intro / verses / instrumentals / bridge / outro). The shipped example is a worked lo-fi hip-hop caption; edit it rather than starting from an empty box. Specific beats poetic: \"78 BPM, D flat major\" lands, \"dreamy\" alone does not. |\n| **Lyrics** | The words, plus `[Intro]` `[Verse]` `[Chorus]` `[Bridge]` `[Instrumental]` `[Outro]` section tags. **The tags are the only structural instruction the model executes** — the lyric text itself only carries mood. `[Instrumental]` with nothing under it is how you get a section with no singing. |\n\n### Dials\n\n- **max_duration** — target length in seconds, shipped at 60 so the first Run finishes quickly.\n  The model supports up to ~300 s (5 minutes) and can also end a song early on its own. Longer\n  costs more time and more VRAM.\n- **seed** — fix it to reproduce a take, change it for a different one. Same caption and lyrics\n  with a new seed is a new performance, not a variation.\n- **Tiled decode** — ships **on**, which decodes the audio VAE in overlapping tiles and cuts\n  decode VRAM sharply. That is what keeps a long song inside a 24 GB card. Turn it off on a big\n  card for the last bit of quality; the tradeoff is a small risk of a seam at a tile boundary.\n- **cfg_scale / top_k** — inside the subgraph, advanced. Leave them alone unless a result is\n  consistently over- or under-cooked.\n\n### Where the files go\n\nSongs are written to the bucket root, so the storage API's `listFiles` (top-level files only)\ncan see them — the same reason the video templates save clips there. Without a bucket selected\neverything goes to `/tmp` and is discarded when the service stops, weights included.\n\nPrompt-writing help: MiniMax publishes a caption-rewriting guide at\nhttps://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MiniMax-Music3"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
